DISPUTE CORRESPONDENCE - CONTRACTOR'S LETTERS

Letter No. GL/2024/089
Date: 01.05.2024

To:
The Managing Director,
USCL, Jaipur

Subject: Scope Creep - Additional 65 Acres Added
Reference: Work Order No. USCL/2023-24/Landscape/672

Dear Sir,

We refer to the site possession given on 20.03.2024 for 185 acres township landscaping.
However, we observe that the Project Director has verbally instructed us to include
additional 65 acres in the landscaping scope without a formal Variation Order.

This additional area includes:
- 15 acres of lakefront development
- 30 acres of green belt along township boundary
- 20 acres of community park development

This is a 35% increase in scope and will require additional resources, time, and cost.
We request USCL to immediately issue a formal Variation Order for this additional work.

Per CPWD GCC Clause 12 (Variations), this additional work shall be compensable.

Yours faithfully,
For M/s. Green Landscape Developers Pvt. Ltd.
Project Manager

***

Letter No. GL/2024/145
Date: 01.09.2024

To:
The Managing Director,
USCL, Jaipur

Subject: Extension of Time Request - Scope Creep and Water Issues
Reference: Our Letter No. GL/2024/089 dated 01.05.2024

Dear Sir,

We submit this formal request for Extension of Time (EOT) under CPWD GCC Clause 44:

EOT Request 1: Scope Creep (Additional 65 Acres)
- Additional area: 65 acres (35% increase in scope)
- Additional time required: 6 months
- Additional cost: ₹2.84 Crore

EOT Request 2: Water Shortage
- USCL failed to provide irrigation infrastructure within 3 months of site handover
  (as per contract Clause 16)
- Water shortage affecting plantation survival
- Additional time required: 3 months for remedial measures

Total EOT requested: 9 months

Yours faithfully,
For M/s. Green Landscape Developers Pvt. Ltd.
Director

***

Letter No. GL/2024/189
Date: 01.12.2024

To:
The Managing Director,
USCL, Jaipur

Subject: Water Shortage Notice - Plantation Survival Rate Drop
Reference: Work Order No. USCL/2023-24/Landscape/672

Dear Sir,

We refer to Clause 16 of the Contract which stipulates that USCL shall provide irrigation
infrastructure within 3 months of site handover (i.e., by 20.06.2024).

As of 01.12.2024, adequate irrigation infrastructure has not been provided. This has caused:
- Plantation survival rate to drop to 65% (vs 95% target)
- Damage to 15,000 plants out of 85,000 planted
- Additional cost for replacement: ₹94 Lakh
- Extended maintenance period required

We request USCL to immediately provide irrigation infrastructure or compensate for
the plantation replacement cost as per CPWD GCC Clause 65 (Force Majeure) and
Clause 44 (Employer's Delay).

Yours faithfully,
For M/s. Green Landscape Developers Pvt. Ltd.
Director